# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Line endings, decided here instead of by whoever happened to clone the repo.
#
# Every text file here is stored with LF and `* text=auto` keeps it that way
# whatever an editor writes. What that alone does NOT settle is the WORKING
# TREE: `core.autocrlf=true` is git's Windows default and is what a
# windows-latest runner checks out with, so on that machine the bytes on disk
# are CRLF. tools/release.mjs packs the working tree into the download, and
# v0.1.0's zip shipped bench-ui.sh with CRLF - `/bin/sh` read the shebang as
# `/bin/sh\r` and every Linux user got "bad interpreter: /bin/sh^M".
#
# So the files a program parses are pinned to LF on disk as well, and the zip
# writer normalises them again as it packs (tools/release.mjs, lfOnly). Either
# half alone leaves the hole open for the next file to fall into: attributes
# fix nobody's existing checkout, and the zip writer fixes nothing a user runs
# out of their own clone.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

*            text=auto

*.sh         text eol=lf
*.mjs        text eol=lf
*.cjs        text eol=lf
*.js         text eol=lf
*.json       text eol=lf
*.yml        text eol=lf
*.yaml       text eol=lf
*.md         text eol=lf
*.html       text eol=lf
*.css        text eol=lf
LICENSE      text eol=lf
.gitignore   text eol=lf
.gitattributes text eol=lf

# cmd.exe is the only thing that ever reads these two, and CRLF is its native
# form - it parses a batch file line by line as it runs it, and LF-only files
# are where `goto` and multi-line blocks go wrong.
*.cmd        text eol=crlf
*.bat        text eol=crlf

# Never converted, never diffed as text. The .ico is the app icon both the
# Windows exe and the Linux AppImage are stamped from; the .png are the
# README's screenshots.
*.ico        binary
*.png        binary

# Nothing game-derived is ever committed - .gitignore covers it and the
# release workflow fails on it - but a file that slipped past both must not
# also be corrupted by an end-of-line conversion on its way in.
*.dds        binary
*.pak        binary
*.cdb        binary
*.dat        binary
